/ test/kkscan.k — kkClassify (table scan) == kkClassifyRec (recursive descent).
/
/ kkClassify was a recursive CST descent costing one VM call frame per operator, so a
/ long kernel expression exhausted the frame stack — the cap was 27 ops, and because a
/ nested run swallowed the overflow it returned a WRONG NUMBER rather than an error
/ (.plan/triage.md #24). The scan does the same job in one pass over the CST table and
/ has no depth budget at all.
/
/ Rewriting a correctness-critical classifier deserves a permanent differential test,
/ not a one-off check: kkClassifyRec is kept purely as the reference implementation and
/ this asserts the two agree. If they ever diverge, kk silently accepts or rejects the
/ wrong kernels.
/ Run: ink test/kkscan.k    (CPU only — no device needed)

2: "lib/kk.k"

OK:: 0; NG:: 0
bump: {[b] $[b; OK::OK+1; NG::NG+1]; 0}
rep:  {[f;a;b] `0 0: "FAIL ",($f),"   rec=",($a),"   scan=",($b)}
one:  {[f] a: kkClassifyRec f; b: kkClassify f; bump a~b; $[a~b; 0; rep[f;a;b]]}

/ Accepted elementwise forms, plus every shape kkChk has a rule for, plus forms that
/ must be REJECTED (gather, amend, scatter, adverbs, a nested lambda).
CORPUS: ({2.*x}; {x+y}; {(x+y)*z}; {sqrt x}; {sin sin x}; {$[x<y;y;x]}
  ; {x@y}; {+/x@y}; {|/x@y}; {+/x@WM}; {1.+.25*+/x@NB}
  ; {@[x;I;:;1.+.25*+/x@W]}; {@[x;HI;+;1.]}; {x*2.+x}; {abs[x-y]}
  ; {x%y}; {exp x}; {log 1.+x}; {x,y}; {x&y}; {x|y}; {~x>y}
  ; {(a;b)}; {x'y}; {x\y}; {{x+1}x}; {0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*x})
corp: one' CORPUS

/ A nested lambda must still be REJECTED: only the ROOT lambda row is skipped by the
/ scan, so an inner one is reported like any other unsupported kind.
chkNest: {[] v: kkClassify {{x+1}x}; bump ~v~`}
nest: chkNest[]   / bind: a bare call auto-prints at script top level

/ Depth. The recursive classifier costs a VM frame per operator and DIES on this chain
/ (verified at 3000 ops: rec produces no result, the scan returns in ~125ms). 200 ops is
/ >7x the old 27-op cap, written out literally so the test needs no code generation.
DEEP:: {0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.0001+1.0001*0.00